From: Eric X. Liu <eric@ericxliu.me>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:06:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] draw/vulkan: do not treat GuestWriteVerdict::NoStamp as a guest write on Load

As documented in `surface_currency.rs`, only `GuestWriteVerdict::Wrote` is
evidence of a guest CPU write; `GuestWriteVerdict::NoStamp` merely means no
dirty-page tracking stamp was armed for the mapping.

In `mapper_ref_texture_guest_wrote_since_store()`, treating `NoStamp` as
`true` caused the attachment LOAD path to discard a valid GPU-resident
surface (whose `resident_content_epoch == mapping_epoch`) and re-seed from
guest RAM. With `REIMS_VGPU_LAZY_WRITEBACK=on` on discrete NVIDIA GPUs
(steelbrain/reims-vgpu#101), those guest pages were never written, turning
composited desktop regions black and forcing users to set
`REIMS_VGPU_LAZY_WRITEBACK=off` (~1.2 GB/s of eager PCIe GPU->CPU readbacks).

Return `false` for `GuestWriteVerdict::NoStamp` while still rejecting
`Wrote`, `NoMapping`, and `Unreadable`.
---
 crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/draw/vulkan.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/draw/vulkan.rs b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/draw/vulkan.rs
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/draw/vulkan.rs
+++ b/crates/reims-vgpu/src/runtime/draw/vulkan.rs
@@ -10143,7 +10143,7 @@ pub(super) fn mapper_ref_texture_guest_wrote_since_store<M: HostOps>(
         }
         GuestWriteVerdict::NoStamp => {
             crate::runtime::drain::note_store_route("t11_gw_ref_no_stamp");
-            true
+            false
         }
         GuestWriteVerdict::Wrote => {
             crate::runtime::drain::note_store_route("t11_gw_ref_moved");
-- 
